// TUDOR glyphs for the Black Bay Pro M79470 (shared by its builders: dial, case, rotor,
// bridges). Vector outlines in local millimetres, so they stay crisp at any zoom and can be
// printed on a canvas or extruded/engraved as 3-D relief:
//
//   - the Tudor SHIELD logo (crenellated top with two horns and a centre merlon, two square
//     windows, the open lower field, pointed base) and the serif TUDOR wordmark and the
//     condensed GENEVE, TRACED from the official dial macro (img/tudor-m79470/off_feat_dial.png,
//     ≈178 px/mm) and registered on the dial with an affine fitted to the measured letter
//     boxes of the 4000 px press image (research/tudor-m79470/exterior.md §3.5): letter edges
//     land within ≈0.03 mm of the measured boxes; the shield is mirror-averaged about its axis;
//   - the heraldic TUDOR ROSE (crown end, relief), built parametrically to the proportions
//     measured on the rectified crown macros (press_M79470-0004_DET_RGB.png, off_feat_bezel.png):
//     five barbed sepals between five outer petals drawn as raised rims round a slot, the
//     inner five-pointed rose (points at the outer petals' centres) with a groove round the
//     raised centre disc, and a small centre seed.
//
// A REGION is { outer: [[x, y], …] (counter-clockwise), holes: [[[x, y], …] (clockwise), …] };
// glyph functions return arrays of regions in a local frame (+y = glyph up). Use
//   drawRegions(ctx2d, regions)          fill on a 2-D canvas (even-odd holes; the canvas
//                                        transform maps local mm → px, y up or down)
//   regionsToShapes(THREE, regions)      THREE.Shape[] for ExtrudeGeometry / ShapeGeometry
//   mapRegions(regions, (x, y) => [x', y'])   any placement (rotate, mirror for back-view text,
//                                        wrap round an arc …); mirroring flips the winding, so
//                                        mapRegions re-orients outers CCW / holes CW
//   regionsToOps(regions) + runOps(g, ops)   ops in the nomos-glyphs style ({ fill, holes })
// Exports are stable: SHIELD_SIZE, TUDOR_CAP, GENEVE_CAP, DIAL_PRINT, shieldRegions,
// tudorRegions, tudorLetterRegions, genevaRegions, dialTextRegions, roseRegions, ROSE, regionsToOps, runOps,
// drawRegions, regionsToShapes, mapRegions, regionBounds, polygonArea, meshStarRegion, distToPolygon,
// pointInPolygon, resamplePolygon.

